  "editorial_note": "GitHub listed twelve projects this Saturday morning; four of them were featured here in the past week and stay out. Today's seven picks are all first appearances: Alibaba's ==AI code reviewer that tops the list==, Tailscale's ==netcat over WireGuard without an account==, Chrome DevTools for coding agents, the self-hosted monitor Uptime Kuma, Block's agent workspace Buzz, the agent review surface Plannotator and a set of Claude trading-process skills. Curation order reflects practical interest, not GitHub rank. Trending is not a release date or an endorsement.",
  "coverage_notes": [
    "GitHub's daily listing held 12 rows at capture. The capture parsed exactly twelve listing rows and is GitHub's own list, not a truncation by us.",
    "All 12 listing entries were inspected. Exact public GitHub API metadata and README files of the eight new candidates were read between 07:01:10 and 07:01:19 UTC, and recent releases at about 07:01:45 UTC. Every checked repository was active and unarchived.",
    "Four entries featured in the past seven days were left out without a new primary-sourced reason: ZhuLinsen/daily_stock_analysis (10 November), we-promise/sure (11 November), and GoogleChrome/modern-web-guidance-src and openai/codex-security (12 November). None has a release since its pick that we judged a material change.",
    "Likely7/Veyra-NRVideo (GPL-3.0, Windows video enhancement) was not picked: its listing line promises '120FPS with DLSS 5' for a console game, a marketing claim we could not verify from primary sources.",
    "The preceding seven calendar dates, 7-13 November, were checked for local history; all seven editions exist.",
    "The official listing was captured at 08:00:57 Europe/Paris. Literal stars-today labels are GitHub's displayed period figures; API total stars and README evidence were checked separately at the times shown per card. They are not an independently audited rolling 24-hour growth measurement.",
    "Feature descriptions, benchmark, adoption and performance figures come from each project's own README and release notes and are the maintainers' claims. No candidate code, installer, CLI, app, skill or model was installed, downloaded or run, and none of this is a security audit or endorsement."
