      "repository": "alibaba/open-code-review",
      "url": "https://github.com/alibaba/open-code-review",
      "trending_rank": 1,
      "description": "A command-line AI code reviewer from Alibaba: it reads a Git diff, hands the changed files to an LLM agent with code-search tools, and returns line-level review comments, with built-in rules for defects such as null dereferences, thread safety, XSS and SQL injection.",
      "why_interesting": "It ==fences the LLM inside deterministic steps==: ordinary code picks which files to review, bundles related files, matches rules and pins each comment to a line, and the model only reasons inside each bundle. The README says it began as Alibaba's internal review assistant and publishes its own 200-PR benchmark against a general-purpose agent, claiming higher precision at about a ninth of the tokens; those are maintainer figures.",
      "caveat": "Outside its delegation mode it ==sends your changed code to the LLM provider you configure==, with that provider's costs and data terms. The README itself says its recall is lower than a general-purpose agent by design, so it can miss defects; it is a second reader, not a security audit.",
      "category": "Developer tools / AI code review",
      "language": "Go",
      "license": "Apache-2.0",
      "stars_total": 50847,
      "stars_period": 215,
      "stars_period_label": "215 stars today",
