    {
      "repository": "tailscale/tailcat",
      "url": "https://github.com/tailscale/tailcat",
      "trending_rank": 10,
      "description": "A netcat-style CLI and Go library from Tailscale that connects two machines over Tailscale's WireGuard data plane without its control plane: one side listens and prints a short address, the other connects with it, and traffic is end-to-end encrypted.",
      "why_interesting": "You get NAT traversal and ==encrypted point-to-point pipes with no account and no root==: it runs in userspace, leaves routing and DNS alone, and exchanges connection details however you like. It can pipe files, forward ports or serve SSH, and an experimental WebAssembly demo talks to the CLI from a browser.",
      "caveat": "The ==address is the credential==: anyone who learns it can connect, and the README warns that a no-auth SSH server turns a leaked address into a shell. Saved keys keep the address valid across restarts, and the default public DERP relays are rate-limited, so heavy relayed traffic needs your own relay.",
      "category": "Networking / command-line tool",
      "language": "Go",
      "license": "BSD-3-Clause",
      "stars_total": 9575,
