      "description": "The Chrome DevTools team's MCP server and CLI that lets a coding agent drive and inspect a live Chrome browser: record performance traces, read network requests and console messages with source-mapped stack traces, take screenshots and automate pages through Puppeteer.",
      "why_interesting": "Agents that write front-end code usually cannot see what the page does; this gives them ==the same traces and network panel a developer uses==, maintained under the ChromeDevTools organisation. Version 1.13.0 shipped on 11 November.",
