      "repository": "block/buzz",
      "url": "https://github.com/block/buzz",
      "trending_rank": 8,
      "description": "Block's self-hostable team workspace where people and AI agents share the same channels; under the hood it is a Nostr relay, so every message, reaction, workflow step, review approval and Git patch is a signed event in one log. This repo holds the relay and the mobile client.",
      "why_interesting": "Instead of bolting bots onto chat, it ==gives agents their own keys, channel memberships and audit trail==, the same as a human member, so what an agent did is recorded and searchable next to the patch and the approval. A new desktop release, 0.5.30, landed early on 14 November.",
      "caveat": "Releases are still ==0.x, and the desktop app lives in a separate repo==. A production setup means running Postgres, Redis and object storage yourself, and the agent capabilities described in the README are the maintainers' vision, not something we tested.",
