      "repository": "backnotprop/plannotator",
      "url": "https://github.com/backnotprop/plannotator",
      "trending_rank": 6,
      "description": "A local, browser-based review surface for AI coding agents such as Claude Code, Codex, Copilot CLI, Gemini CLI and OpenCode: when the agent proposes a plan or finishes work, you annotate the plan, document or diff in the browser and send the feedback straight back to the agent.",
      "why_interesting": "It turns agent oversight into ==commenting on a plan or diff instead of typing corrections==, and it covers Git, Jujutsu, Perforce, GitHub and GitLab reviews. Its README has a clear privacy section: no telemetry, and content stays local unless you use a sharing or hosted feature.",
      "caveat": "It ==installs through your agent's plugins, hooks and commands==, so it changes how your agent sessions run; review what it adds first. Shared links leave your machine (encrypted short links upload ciphertext to a paste service), the hosted Workspaces product is separate, and releases are still 0.x.",
